#: archimage-cli
msgctxt "archimage-cli"
msgid ""
"ArchImage is the bundling of Arch Linux packages into an AppImage using "
"JuNest.\n"
" \n"
" This allows you to use the latest programs from Arch Linux and AUR on "
"every  distribution, old or newer.\n"
" \n"
" In the past AppImages were built using .deb packages or guessing "
"instructions  to make them work. With the \"ArchImage\" method all you have "
"to do is the  reverse, i.e. \"delete\" what is no longer needed.\n"
" \n"
" Among the advantages, we have:\n"
" - compatibility with all versions of Linux starting from kernel 2.6, "
"therefore  also older distributions than those normally indicated by the "
"classic AppImage  developers;\n"
" - easy and immediate compilation;\n"
" - AppRun script very minimal and easy to configure;\n"
" - all programs for Arch Linux within AppImage's reach, therefore one of "
"the  most extensive software parks in the GNU/Linux panorama.\n"
" \n"
" This tool is a part of \"AM\" and AppMan and many AppImages built to "
"complete this collection (like obs-studio, mpv, abiword and handbrake) are "
"built using this solution.\n"
" \n"
" To learn more visit the main repo of this project."
msgstr ""
"ArchImage is the bundling of Arch Linux packages into an AppImage using "
"JuNest.\n"
" \n"
" This allows you to use the latest programs from Arch Linux and AUR on "
"every  distribution, old or newer.\n"
" \n"
" In the past AppImages were built using .deb packages or guessing "
"instructions  to make them work. With the \"ArchImage\" method all you have "
"to do is the  reverse, i.e. \"delete\" what is no longer needed.\n"
" \n"
" Among the advantages, we have:\n"
" - compatibility with all versions of Linux starting from kernel 2.6, "
"therefore  also older distributions than those normally indicated by the "
"classic AppImage  developers;\n"
" - easy and immediate compilation;\n"
" - AppRun script very minimal and easy to configure;\n"
" - all programs for Arch Linux within AppImage's reach, therefore one of "
"the  most extensive software parks in the GNU/Linux panorama.\n"
" \n"
" This tool is a part of \"AM\" and AppMan and many AppImages built to "
"complete this collection (like obs-studio, mpv, abiword and handbrake) are "
"built using this solution.\n"
" \n"
" To learn more visit the main repo of this project."

