#: inkscape
msgctxt "inkscape"
msgid ""
"Inkscape is a Free and open source vector graphics editor for GNU/Linux, "
"Windows and MacOS X. It offers a rich set of features and is widely used for "
"both artistic and technical illustrations such as cartoons, clip art, logos, "
"typography, diagramming and flowcharting. It uses vector graphics to allow "
"for sharp printouts and renderings at unlimited resolution and is not bound "
"to a fixed number of pixels like raster graphics. Inkscape uses the "
"standardized SVG file format as its main format, which is supported by many "
"other applications including web browsers.\n"
" \n"
" It can import and export various file formats, including SVG, AI, EPS, PDF, "
"PS and PNG. It has a comprehensive feature set, a simple interface, multi-"
"lingual support and is designed to be extensible; users can customize "
"Inkscape's functionality with add-ons.\n"
"\n"
" This is the unofficial Archimage built on top of JuNest."
msgstr ""
"Inkscape is a Free and open source vector graphics editor for GNU/Linux, "
"Windows and MacOS X. It offers a rich set of features and is widely used for "
"both artistic and technical illustrations such as cartoons, clip art, logos, "
"typography, diagramming and flowcharting. It uses vector graphics to allow "
"for sharp printouts and renderings at unlimited resolution and is not bound "
"to a fixed number of pixels like raster graphics. Inkscape uses the "
"standardized SVG file format as its main format, which is supported by many "
"other applications including web browsers.\n"
" \n"
" It can import and export various file formats, including SVG, AI, EPS, PDF, "
"PS and PNG. It has a comprehensive feature set, a simple interface, multi-"
"lingual support and is designed to be extensible; users can customize "
"Inkscape's functionality with add-ons.\n"
"\n"
" This is the unofficial Archimage built on top of JuNest."

