#: kigo
msgctxt "kigo"
msgid ""
"Kigo is an open-source implementation of the popular Go game. Go is a "
"strategic board game for two players. It is also known as igo (Japanese), "
"weiqi or wei  ch'i (Chinese) or baduk (Korean). \n"
" \n"
" Go is noted for being rich in strategic complexity despite its simple "
"rules.  The game is played by two players who alternately place black and "
"white stones  (playing pieces, now usually made of glass or plastic) on the "
"vacant  intersections of a grid of 19x19 lines (9x9 or 13x13 for easier "
"games).\n"
" \n"
" This game is part of the KDE Games suite.\n"
" \n"
" USAGE (from the command line):\n"
" \n"
"           kdegames -h (shows the list of games)\n"
"           kdegames $GAME (launches the selected game)"
msgstr ""
